    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d907">

                <pb facs="0971" n="959" xml:id="pg959"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 P.W./6–745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-07T19:00:00+02:00">June 7, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 7—2:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5758. Your 4527, June 6.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d907-f1"/> We asked the ForOff
                    today whether it had reached any decision on Italian declaration of war on
                    Japan. An official told us that the delay in reaching a decision had been caused
                    by the necessity of asking the opinions of the Dominions govts and that the Emb
                    can expect to have a reply “within a week”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
